  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Worktree for DSH",
      "text": "> List git worktrees read-only in DSH; create/remove/prune via CLI for isolated experiments."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "```bash\nnode bin/dsh-worktree.mjs list --root .\nnode bin/dsh-worktree.mjs create --root . --path ../exp --branch exp-1\nnode bin/dsh-worktree.mjs remove --root . --path ../exp\nnode bin/dsh-worktree.mjs prune --root .\n\nIn DSH:\n\n```text\nUse worktree_list on this repository.\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Safety",
      "text": "- Read-only DSH tool; create/remove are CLI-only.\n- Refuses existing target path and unsafe branch names.\n- `remove` refuses dirty worktrees unless `--force`.\n- No branch deletion, no test execution."
    }
